{"book":"lines-angles","bookTitle":"Lines and angles","concept":8,"title":"Angles in a triangle","grades":"Grades 7–8","goal":"I can use the angle sum and the exterior angle of a triangle.","teach":"The angles of a triangle add up to <b>180°</b>. An <b>exterior angle</b> (made by extending one side) equals the sum of the two <b>opposite interior angles</b>. In an <b>isosceles</b> triangle the angles opposite the equal sides are equal. Each angle of an <b>equilateral</b> triangle is 60°.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:437px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 336 194\"><g transform=\"translate(14.0,6.0)\"><line x1=\"20.0\" y1=\"150.0\" x2=\"215.0\" y2=\"150.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"215.0\" y1=\"150.0\" x2=\"95.0\" y2=\"30.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"95.0\" y1=\"30.0\" x2=\"20.0\" y2=\"150.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"215.0\" y1=\"150.0\" x2=\"290.0\" y2=\"150.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M46.0,150.0 A26,26 0 0 0 33.8,128.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"57.3\" y=\"133.8\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">50°</text><path d=\"M196.6,131.6 A26,26 0 0 0 189.0,150.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"175.6\" y=\"138.2\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">70°</text><path d=\"M83.3,48.7 A22,22 0 0 0 110.6,45.6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"99.4\" y=\"72.9\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">60°</text><path d=\"M237.0,150.0 A22,22 0 0 0 199.4,134.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"231.5\" y=\"114.8\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">110°</text><text x=\"8.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A</text><text x=\"223.0\" y=\"171.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">B</text><text x=\"95.0\" y=\"21.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">C</text><text x=\"300.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">D</text></g></svg></span><div class=\"cap\">50° + 70° + 60° = 180°. The exterior angle at B is 50° + 60° = 110°.</div></div>","ex":{"q":"A triangle has angles 50° and 65°. Find the third angle.","steps":["The angles of a triangle add up to 180°.","50° + 65° + x = 180°, so 115° + x = 180°.","x = 65°."]},"watch":"The exterior angle equals the two interior angles <b>opposite</b> it, not the one next to it.","qs":[{"text":"Find x.","vis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:337px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 259 194\"><g transform=\"translate(14.0,6.0)\"><line x1=\"20.0\" y1=\"150.0\" x2=\"215.0\" y2=\"150.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"215.0\" y1=\"150.0\" x2=\"95.0\" y2=\"30.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"95.0\" y1=\"30.0\" x2=\"20.0\" y2=\"150.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M46.0,150.0 A26,26 0 0 0 33.8,128.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"57.3\" y=\"133.8\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">70°</text><path d=\"M196.6,131.6 A26,26 0 0 0 189.0,150.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"175.6\" y=\"138.2\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" 