"65.1\" y2=\"88.1\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"134.9\" y1=\"88.1\" x2=\"145.1\" y2=\"81.9\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"8.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A</text><text x=\"188.0\" y=\"171.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">B</text><text x=\"100.0\" y=\"11.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">C</text></g></svg></span></div>","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"x (°)","a":"70","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"(180 − 40) ÷ 2","steps":"1. Rule: in an isosceles triangle, the two base angles (opposite the equal sides) are equal.<br>2. Rule: the three angles of a triangle add up to 180°.<br>3. x = (180° − 40°) ÷ 2<br>4. = 140° ÷ 2 = 70°"}]}